[ ] Derive all-day and floating occurrence ids the same on every device =slot-key-zone $Found 2026-10-12 drafting spec-habits. canonical_occurrence_key in crates/clearhead-core/src/workspace/calendar/ics.rs converts the slot from the machine's local zone to UTC, so a date-only or floating slot keys differently on devices in different zones, and so does the occurrence id derived from it. That breaks Decision 56's 'every device computes the same id'. The code comment calls floating 'the acknowledged edge', but all-day Habits are common. Likely fix: key date-only slots as a date and floating ones as written, not as UTC instants. The ics_schedule_spec.md canonical RECURRENCE-ID wording (spec-habits) should state it, and app:slot's type in ontology.md would follow.$ !2 ^2026-10-12T03:11 #01a12e18-2187-7253-ad5d-d85e70bf8bc7
